      "mode": "multiple",
      "domain": "Real numbers, explicitly stated in the view.",
      "independent_solution": "For (I), x^2-2x=35; adding 1 gives (x-1)^2=36, hence x=1+6 or 1-6, so {-5,7}. For (II), x^2+8x=20; adding 16 gives (x+4)^2=36, hence x=-4+6 or -4-6, so {-10,2}. Each positive square equation has exactly two real branches.",
